==Tocharian B==

===Etymology===
From Proto-Tocharian *''meim'', a nominal derivative of *''mei-'' ("to measure"). Possibly linked to {{etyl|ine-pro|txb}} *''mod-ye/o-'' or *''mēdye/o-'', derivatives of {{recons|med-||to measure, give advice, heal|lang=ine-pro}} (whence Latin {{term|meditor|lang=la}}), or alternatively to *''meh₁-ye/o-'' from {{recons|meh₁-||to measure|lang=ine-pro}} (whence Latin {{term|metior|mētior|lang=la}}). Compare Tocharian A {{term|mem|lang=xto}}.

